============================================================
MACHINE LEARNING + FLASK
SIMPLE INDUSTRIAL PROJECT ASSIGNMENT
====================================

## PROJECT TITLE

Concrete Strength Prediction System

============================================================

1. PROJECT SCENARIO
   ============================================================

A construction company wants to use Machine Learning to
predict the compressive strength of concrete.

You will build a simple Machine Learning system that:

Concrete Ingredients → Machine Learning Model → Concrete Strength

The final prediction will be available through a Flask
web application.

============================================================
2. DATASET
==========

Use the:

"Concrete Compressive Strength Dataset" 
Find dataset by yourself if you cannot then use give below link of dataset:
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/elikplim/concrete-compressive-strength-data-set

The dataset contains information about concrete ingredients
and the resulting concrete strength.

## INPUT FEATURES

1. Cement
2. Blast Furnace Slag
3. Fly Ash
4. Water
5. Superplasticizer
6. Coarse Aggregate
7. Fine Aggregate
8. Age

## TARGET

Concrete Compressive Strength

============================================================
3. PROJECT TASKS
================

Complete the following 7 steps.

---

## STEP 1 — LOAD DATASET

Load the dataset using Pandas.

Check the following:

1. First 5 rows
2. Number of rows and columns
3. Column names
4. Missing values

---

## STEP 2 — PREPARE DATA

Separate the data into:

X = Input Features

y = Concrete Strength

Then divide the data into:

80% Training Data

20% Testing Data

---

## STEP 3 — TRAIN REGRESSION MODELS

Train 3 regression models that you learned in class.

For example:

1. Linear Regression
2. Decision Tree Regression
3. Random Forest Regression

You may choose other regression models from the models
taught in class.

---

## STEP 4 — EVALUATE MODELS

Calculate the following:

1. MAE
2. RMSE
3. R² Score

Create a comparison of the three models.

Compare the results and select one model for the final
application.

---

## STEP 5 — SAVE THE MODEL

Save your selected model using Joblib.

Example:

import joblib

joblib.dump(model, "concrete_model.pkl")

Your project must contain:

concrete_model.pkl

---

## STEP 6 — CREATE FLASK APPLICATION

Create a Flask application that:

1. Loads concrete_model.pkl
2. Takes concrete information from the user
3. Sends the information to the model
4. Generates a prediction
5. Displays the predicted concrete strength

---

## STEP 7 — CREATE WEB PAGE

Create a simple HTML page with input fields for:

1. Cement
2. Blast Furnace Slag
3. Fly Ash
4. Water
5. Superplasticizer
6. Coarse Aggregate
7. Fine Aggregate
8. Age

Add a:

Predict Strength

button.

After clicking the button, display:

Predicted Concrete Strength:

XX.XX MPa

